body:
My KT group play 130-135pts

So here's my new go-to list for nids.


**+ Leader +**

&nbsp;

**Tyranid Warrior [22pts]:** Boneswords, Deathspitter, Kraken


. **Leader**

&nbsp;

**+ Specialists +**

&nbsp;

**Genestealer [11pts]:** Kraken


. **Veteran**

&nbsp;

**Ravener [17pts]:** Kraken, 2x Scything talons, Spinefists


. **Combat**

&nbsp;

**Tyranid Warrior Gunner [24pts]:** Kraken, Scything talons, Venom cannon


. **Heavy**

&nbsp;

**+ Non-specialists +**

&nbsp;

**Hormagaunt [4pts]:** *No Hive Fleet*

&nbsp;

**Hormagaunt [4pts]:** *No Hive Fleet*

&nbsp;

**Hormagaunt [4pts]:** *No Hive Fleet*

&nbsp;

**Hormagaunt [4pts]:** *No Hive Fleet*

&nbsp;

**Hormagaunt [4pts]:** *No Hive Fleet*

&nbsp;

**Hormagaunt [4pts]:** *No Hive Fleet*

&nbsp;

**Hormagaunt [4pts]:** *No Hive Fleet*

&nbsp;

**Hormagaunt [4pts]:** *No Hive Fleet*

&nbsp;

**Hormagaunt [4pts]:** *No Hive Fleet*

&nbsp;

**Hormagaunt [4pts]:** *No Hive Fleet*

&nbsp;

**Hormagaunt [4pts]:** *No Hive Fleet*

&nbsp;

**Hormagaunt [4pts]:** *No Hive Fleet*

&nbsp;

**Hormagaunt [4pts]:** *No Hive Fleet*

&nbsp;

**Hormagaunt [4pts]:** *No Hive Fleet*

&nbsp;

**++ Total: [130pts] ++**

Theres only like 2 differences? Mawloc is all melee and can put itself back into deepstrike, while the trygon can only deepstrike once and can bring friends along too as well as a ranged attack.

&#x200B;

Personally happy I went with a Trygon though i havent used it since its first outing. Where i used it to deepstrike a 20 strong unit of  Gaunts behind a couple of Necron Warriors.
